Z||000003||Songman||04-10-2001||08:10 AM||||I love em! I especially love the shaved moldings and the side openings. Now that is the style someone needs to build. You glass guys, there's your project!<P>So we're all talking shaved molding these days. And yeah, parking lots could be a problem, but no more so than for a lot of cars out there that don't have molding from the factory, et al: Hurst Olds never had molding but there are a lot of them out there...<P>I would love to do this... but the thing that I am having trouble with is this. You would really have to destry your car if someone back into your rear bumper or something. No more easy to fix Fiero. But again, I guess that is no different than a lot of cars out there.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||AusFiero||04-10-2001||10:22 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>I love em! I especially love the shaved moldings and the side openings. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The side openings are 1998 Corvette front guard openings, mirrored and extended in height to suit the Fiero.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||04-10-2001||11:07 AM||||Sweet!<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||14
