Z||000007||Monkeyman||04-11-2001||04:58 AM||||What?!  No notchbacks?  I'm upset now.  I would go in a corner and cry, but I'm just too shallow to let that bother me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Seriously, how about some modified notchbacks?  Stock wing (with slightly taller stands) and the Vette side scoops, please.<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000008||COUNTIBLIS||04-11-2001||09:42 AM||||So what all would need to be done to make a Fiero look like that?  That is sweet, I like the look of the 90's Z.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||AusFiero||04-11-2001||09:46 AM||||To get that look fabricate and mould on a lip spoiler...make new lower panels and doorskins with the scoops and smooth over the body mouldings.<BR>No other body mods done to them ones.||||reg||1
Z||000010||AusFiero||04-11-2001||10:15 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>You would really have to destry your car if someone back into your rear bumper or something. No more easy to fix Fiero<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The way around that songman would be to leave the rear bumper as an individual unit and instead of making new moulded panels make only lower ones that join flush along the new bodyline. Keeps all the panels separate. Standard Fiero upper sail panels, nose, rear bumper, boot, and front guards could all be retained with a small variation of this design.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Haze_Performance||04-11-2001||11:16 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero004.jpg">  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I always wondered why no one ever made the side scoop & door skin like that?? I would also love to have open 1/4 windows..  <BR><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze8588logo.gif">  </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A>||||reg||14
Z||000012||AusFiero||04-11-2001||07:44 PM||||Ok I am seriously considering manufacturing the red one (Have a past in fibreglass fabrication, and design so it isn't out of my realm). Would there be much interest in a bodykit if I could send them to America? (already have shipping contacts). The Aussie Dollar is worth about a Peso so I am sure I could make them very cost competitively. For shipping logistics reasons I would rather sell direct to a parts or performance dealer though, preferably based near LA as that is where I can ship to easily and cheaply.<P>Much interest in this to justify my expenses?||||reg||1
Z||000013||BAM-BAM||04-11-2001||08:15 PM||||  I would certainly be interested in those doors and scoops. I really like the short fin on the decklid. That is some awesome artistic impressionism. Perhaps if you patented the proccess You could sell the pattent to an iterprising Fiero nut stateside that could produce them even cheaper in the home market. You might be hard pressed otherwise with the incurred shipping costs. I say either way, GO FOR IT!!!!.<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Knowledge is POWER!<BR>That is why the ignorant remain Weak!||||reg||12
