Z||000017||Haze_Performance||04-12-2001||02:47 AM||||I like the door & scoops.. I see only 1 problem. The scoops seem do-able but the door skins might be hard. If you recess them to much, it may interfere with the insides of the door & door frame. (Window going down ect..) But if you were able to make them, I would be interested..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze8588logo.gif">  </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A>||||reg||10
Z||000018||AusFiero||04-12-2001||04:49 AM||||Already worked out the door inner frame bit. It stays near stock with a 1cm deep chunk out of the scoop area. As far as I can see this won't affect anything. The scoops door depth is actually just over replacing the thickness of the original GT door skirts. The scoops themselves are no problem. Will work out more of the logistics of it as I go.||||reg||1
