Z||000022||AusFiero||04-16-2001||08:52 AM||||Ok I am going to build it. Was at the Pontiac nats this weekend and a fellow Aussie Fiero enthusiast "Allan McCelland - owner of the The Fiero Shop Australia" has offered me a 1988 GT 5 speed with factory option t-tops. It is a bit run down "ideal for this project" but at $6500 (about $3200 US)it is a great buy as it is already converted to RHD. <P>Allan's Fiero Shop specialises in fitting local Holden 3.8 ltr  V6 engines into Fieros. So with that in mind the plans are to include a twin turboed 3.8 ltr with hopefully at least 300 HP to the back wheels. Am also considering ABS brakes off the same donor vehicle the engine comes out of "Holden Commodore". This would open the wheel options up to include the Corvette rims and make spare parts supply easier for my part of the word.<P>Otherwise the body is going to stay as it looks above, including the open 1/4 windows. Colour? Who knows as this is going to be a 2 year project to get ready for the next Pontiac Nationals and I might have a favoured shade at that time.<P>Interior wise I am going to go extreme and basically replace the lot with an interior resembling more the interior of a fighter plane or space ship. Sketches underway already. Or my current new interior is at <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006816.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006816.html</A> <P>Now I just have to sell my t-topped 86 GT to start financing the project.||||reg||14
Z||000023||FieroSEt||04-17-2001||11:43 PM||||Hey....  I love all the idea's...  I'm working on the shaved molding as we speak. I'm also shaving the mirror's, and the exhaust holes in the rear fascia. I'm also blending (fiberglassing) in the ground f/x., the sail scoop's and side scoop's, along with the ZR-1 hood scoop. I hope to be finished with the turbo upgrade this summer too. lol....  I now need to think about the door skin idea too.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>Keep up the good work, I hope to get a digital cam. in the next few week's so I can post some pic's.( hopefully when Loki get's back to Texas He can take some with his)<BR>                             Steve<P>------------------<BR>aka... 1FieroGTRacingInc.<BR>       Tyler,Texas<BR>Fiero_87GT@Yahoo.com||||reg||6
